      model_answer: 'We understand why Bell’s association matters to the collection and to the loan. We propose: “Harbour plan, 1894, traditionally attributed to E. Bell in the lending collection.” The wording preserves the history of the attribution and gives visitors a clear name to follow up. The surviving payment record cannot confirm that Bell drew this particular sheet, so we cannot retain the more categorical credit in our own voice. We will send you the specialist’s findings after opening, alongside any proposed revision. In the meantime, the lender’s account of how the map entered the collection can still appear in the adjacent display text.',
