      model_answer: 'I would allocate 50 inspections to each court initially and select addresses randomly within blocks, with a deliberate sample of households that have not reported a fault. The complaint totals can compare recorded demand, but North’s campaign and web form give households a different chance to report than South’s daytime phone line. The earlier visits were selected from existing reporters, so they shed little light on silent demand. Collect comparable inspection outcomes and document refusals in both courts. If the new inspections show a clear difference in verified faults within comparable blocks, reallocate part of the follow-up repair capacity while retaining a basic response in both courts. Keep urgent individual cases outside the sample so they can be assessed promptly.',
