      model_answer: 'The draft is ambiguous because Park treats registration as the threshold for active membership, while River asks for a completed shift in the last 60 days. Under River’s reading, a newly registered person or a member returning after three months could lose the swap route even though the merger group agreed they should have it. Replace the clause with “Anyone registered with the co-operative can request a shift swap.” If the scheduler needs to track recent participation for another purpose, give that status a separate name and define the time window there. That keeps the report useful without changing who can request a swap.',
