      model_answer: 'Use source definitions only for rows where the originating group is known. For a comparable attendance series, use the independent check-in timestamps since June and check both groups use the same timezone and shift identifiers. Keep old rows with an unknown origin unclassified rather than inferring a definition from their values. We may be able to publish separate pre-June figures for each group, provided the definitions and available coverage appear next to them. Caption: “Recorded check-ins since June across the two co-operatives. Earlier records use different status definitions and are excluded from this chart.” Keep the older information accessible in the supporting notes, so readers understand which part of the year the chart can actually describe.',
